2026-09-26 — K12 splice module prerequisite; reference-only runtime evidence.

The retained September 22 full run fails splice:short_splice_read.sh on BOTH
Images: modprobe cannot find test_module, then the two sysfs paths do not exist.
Earlier proc/sys splice checks already succeed. CONFIG_TEST_LKM=m in the reviewed
new configuration builds the exact lib/test_module.ko required by this script.

module-sysfs-splice.c, built with sealed GCC14 -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror,
runs on the new matching GCC Image. It observes the missing path before load,
loads a newly signed COPY of that Image's module, compares full and two-byte
splice against read for coresize and sections/.init.text, then runs the original
unchanged script and helper. A five-second alarm preserves splice/settings's
original limit. It unloads the module and checks that the path disappears again.
All 8 diagnostic assertions PASS; original shell exit 0; boot/shutdown PASS.
The missing-module prerequisite has a causal reference control, not merely
equal failure counts. New EvoCC Image/module replay remains NOT_RUN while its
uniform build proceeds; neither old full-run totals nor K12 are closed here.

The script/helper, shell/coreutils and libraries were extracted read-only from
the retained matching reference runtime. Only needed files enter a 4,923,904-byte
initramfs. The existing 64 MiB scratch disk is used in snapshot mode and its
hash is unchanged. No full runtime copy or source/kernel mutation was made.
Readelf confirms libc/loader and grep's libpcre2 are the complete dependency set.

Build: container run --rm --platform linux/arm64 --network none --cpus 1
 --memory 1G; fixtures/harness/new reference build mounted read-only, probe
 directory writable; evo-flight-lab:sealed sh /probe/build.sh.
